WEBVTT

00:00.160 --> 00:01.640
Bonus episode.

00:01.640 --> 00:03.399
After UNLEASH I received a great

00:03.399 --> 00:04.560
question.

00:04.560 --> 00:05.920
How do you translate business

00:05.920 --> 00:08.800
strategy into workforce simulations?

00:08.800 --> 00:10.559
Here is workforce intelligence in

00:10.559 --> 00:11.360
practice.

00:11.601 --> 00:13.200
Business needs now change faster

00:13.200 --> 00:15.201
than any annual plan.

00:15.201 --> 00:17.001
And AI is transforming the tasks

00:17.001 --> 00:19.041
themselves. Writing went from

00:19.041 --> 00:21.641
pencil to keyboard to voice. We

00:21.641 --> 00:23.160
can no longer manage people as

00:23.160 --> 00:24.561
static resources.

00:24.842 --> 00:26.721
On the productivity side, faster

00:26.721 --> 00:28.921
decisions, fluid teams and

00:28.921 --> 00:30.762
knowledge kept before experts

00:30.762 --> 00:31.642
retire.

00:31.803 --> 00:34.163
On the cultural side, AI augments

00:34.163 --> 00:36.323
employees. It does not replace

00:36.323 --> 00:38.683
them. But this requires bold

00:38.683 --> 00:40.043
change leaders.

00:40.284 --> 00:42.324
Most companies already do workforce

00:42.324 --> 00:44.403
planning. A plan fixed once a

00:44.403 --> 00:47.124
year, focused on headcount and

00:47.124 --> 00:48.204
reactive.

00:48.404 --> 00:49.445
But the business questions have

00:49.445 --> 00:52.124
changed. Which jobs will we need?

00:52.124 --> 00:53.765
How will AI change them? And how

00:53.765 --> 00:56.165
fast? A headcount plan cannot

00:56.165 --> 00:56.925
answer them.

00:57.285 --> 00:59.926
Our HR systems see job titles,

00:59.926 --> 01:02.646
individual skills, and org charts.

01:02.646 --> 01:04.365
Below the surface are the weak

01:04.365 --> 01:06.966
signals, tacit knowledge, team

01:06.966 --> 01:09.565
dynamics and engagement. Without

01:09.565 --> 01:11.326
them, we cannot see the real

01:11.326 --> 01:13.806
organization or simulate how it

01:13.806 --> 01:15.286
reacts to change.

01:15.567 --> 01:18.087
This data already exists, inside

01:18.087 --> 01:20.126
and outside the company. No extra

01:20.126 --> 01:22.047
data entry for employees.

01:22.528 --> 01:24.648
At the core, a workforce digital

01:24.648 --> 01:26.728
twin connects these signals and

01:26.728 --> 01:28.447
learns their dependencies in a

01:28.447 --> 01:30.568
governed and transparent way.

01:30.569 --> 01:32.968
For example, how will AI change

01:32.968 --> 01:35.249
jobs? The twin breaks each job

01:35.249 --> 01:37.368
into tasks and rates the AI

01:37.368 --> 01:38.569
impact on each one.

01:38.730 --> 01:41.370
Writing job ads and screening CVs,

01:41.370 --> 01:43.929
high AI impact in the short term.

01:43.929 --> 01:46.650
Negotiating offers, lower impact.

01:46.971 --> 01:49.091
Then we redesign the job. The

01:49.091 --> 01:51.930
recruiter becomes a talent advisor.

01:51.930 --> 01:54.410
Less admin, more time with people.

01:54.410 --> 01:56.851
Same authority and accountability.

01:56.851 --> 02:00.450
New task, supervising AI agents.

02:00.450 --> 02:02.571
The skills move, less screening,

02:02.571 --> 02:03.891
more advising.

02:03.891 --> 02:06.171
And a new skill, judging AI

02:06.171 --> 02:06.931
output.

02:07.212 --> 02:09.052
Then the twin scales this across

02:09.052 --> 02:11.132
the organization for each business

02:11.132 --> 02:13.612
scenario. A new product, a new

02:13.612 --> 02:16.292
technology, which jobs change, how

02:16.292 --> 02:19.012
fast, how many people, and which

02:19.012 --> 02:20.172
AI agents.

02:20.372 --> 02:23.533
Four shifts, one operating system.

02:23.533 --> 02:25.972
And now, a concrete way to start.

02:25.972 --> 02:28.772
One critical job, its tasks and

02:28.772 --> 02:30.613
your business scenarios. More

02:30.613 --> 02:31.692
human,

02:31.692 --> 02:35.253
more digital, not a trade-off. AND.

02:35.534 --> 02:36.854
Thank you for watching.
